## style-ok: no-strict - sourced library.

## Single source of truth for legacy-dist 'do_once' marker basenames that are
## shared between the image build and runtime checks, so a rename cannot drift
## between the producer and the consumer.
##
## image_builtin_mok_absent_marker_basename:
##   Producer: the image build (initializer-dist
##     chroot-scripts-post.d/20_sanity_checks) drops this marker, but ONLY after
##     it has PROVEN the image ships no built-in MOK key.
##   Consumer: check-image-builtin-mok short-circuits to "safe" when it is
##     present, treating any MOK key on disk as a legitimate per-machine key
##     generated at runtime, never a shared key leaked through the image.
##   Location: /var/lib/legacy-dist/do_once/<basename>.
## shellcheck: consumed by sourcing scripts, not within this fragment.
# shellcheck disable=SC2034
image_builtin_mok_absent_marker_basename='image_built_without_mok'
